There's a riding spoiler at:
http://www.nethack.de/spoiler330/riding.txt

It looks like the shoes and gloves help you SADDLE the steed, not mount 
it. The chance to ride is

chance = (user level + tameness) / 20

so the easiest way to increase your chance to mount a new horse is to 
feed it first (which increases tameness). Otherwise, just wait until 
you're higher level. It looks like tameness starts at 10 for your pets 
so the chance of successfully mounting the knight's horse on the first 
turn is simply 11/20, just over 50%.

Some other restrictions apply, which will always cause failure:
Restrictions:
   - monster must be saddled.
   - monster must be tame.
   - player's armor must not be rusty or corroded (thoroughly?).
   - player is not levitating (unless at will).
   - player must fit in saddle (not too big or too small).
   - player is not fumbling, glibbering, has no wounded legs.
   - saddle is not cursed
(from the spoiler mentioned above)

Most are pretty obvious but I didn't know the 3rd point. Also, 
apparently being burdened doesn't affect it either. This is a bit hard 
to believe, perhaps I'll do a little testing.

Saddling the pet is considerably more complex.


